      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T22:05:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Follow-up (design): the cap only applies when the caller passes can_self_schedule\u003dtrue. `quads --ls-available` (cli/cli.py action_available) and the web wiki Available page (web/blueprints/wiki.py available_hosts) don\u0027t pass it, so they list uncapped hosts. A user sees a host as free, POSTs a self-schedule, and gets a 400 - the exact surprise the RFE tries to avoid. The doc caveat is honest, but consider having the SS entry points query the capped view (or annotate capped models).",
      "revId": "a14211ec600367df4344bb1c5bbfb5290fdf5957",
