      "writtenOn": "2026-09-25T22:05:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TOCTOU: this capacity check and the create below are not atomic, and there\u0027s no model-level lock (get_hosts_for_update row-locks only the host) or unique constraint. Production runs gunicorn --workers\u003d17 -k gthread (systemd/quads-server.service:14), so two concurrent self-schedules of different hosts of the same model can both read remaining\u003e0 and both commit, pushing the model above N% - which contradicts the RFE\u0027s \"at most N% at any time.\" Same shape at :579 (PATCH) and :834 (batch). This mirrors the existing ssm_host_limit check, so not a regression, but given the RFE promises a hard bound please either serialize the check+insert (per-model advisory lock / with_for_update / in-txn re-check) or leave a `# ponytail:` note that the cap is best-effort under concurrency.",
