      "message": "Population mismatch with the fleet denominator: count_hosts_by_model (host.py:130) excludes retired+broken, but this active count does not filter them. Concrete failure: 2x R660 @50% -\u003e L\u003d1; host A self-scheduled, then A marked broken. Now fleet\u003d1, model_limit\u003dmax(1,0)\u003d1, but A\u0027s live schedule still counts as active\u003d1 -\u003e remaining\u003d0, so the healthy host B is rejected even though 0 healthy R660s are actively self-scheduled. Direction is conservative w.r.t. the cap, but it wrongly rejects a valid self-schedule. Apply the same retired/broken filter here (or drop it from count_hosts_by_model) so numerator and denominator share a basis.",
